course: dictionary
lesson: 1602
title: Cheeky
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words change their meaning depending on who uses them and how. «Cheeky» is one of them. Look at the words around it to find out which meaning fits. «The Cat answered, "I'd rather not."» Answering back like that is what the word is about here.
explain: Adults often call a child cheeky for answering back. When the King tells the Cat, «Don't be impertinent», he means the Cat is being cheeky, which is rude and not respectful. Impertinent is a longer word for the same idea. Ask yourself whether the speaker is cross or teasing.
explain: In stories, cheeky often describes a lively, naughty character who is not cruel. A «cheeky monkey» is a naughty child, but people say it fondly. A «cheeky grin» is playful and a bit mischievous, not angry. The clues in the sentence tell you which feeling is meant.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Cheeky» means rude or not respectful, often in a funny or playful way.
fact: A «cheeky grin» or «cheeky smile» is playful and a bit naughty.
fact: In British slang, «a cheeky» means a small treat you shouldn't really have, like «a cheeky biscuit».
fact: Useful phrases: «cheeky monkey» (a naughty child, said fondly) and «don't be cheeky» (don't answer back rudely).
exercise: «Don't be impertinent», says the King. What does impertinent mean here? | Hungry and tired | *Cheeky, or rude | Sleepy after a long day | Very kind and helpful
exercise: A big sister smiles and says to her little brother, «You cheeky monkey!» What does it mean? | *A naughty child, said fondly | A wild animal from the zoo | A very angry person who wants to go home | A kind teacher who gives prizes
exercise: Ali eats a biscuit before dinner and says it was «a cheeky biscuit». What does cheeky mean here? | A biscuit that has gone burnt | A rude word for a biscuit | A biscuit that is very big and heavy | *A small treat you shouldn't really have
exercise: Which word means playful and a bit naughty in «a cheeky grin»? | *cheeky | cheeky and grin both mean the same thing exactly | grin | smile is the only word, so there is no clue
test: «Don't be cheeky», the teacher says to a pupil who answered back. What does cheeky mean? | Lost in thought | Very quiet | *Rude or not respectful | Very clever
test: «He gave me a cheeky grin.» What kind of grin is it? | Sad and tired | Very old and faded | *Playful and a bit naughty | Angry and loud
exam: Mum smiles and says, «You're a cheeky so-and-so!» What does she mean? | You are very tired and should go to bed | *You're being naughty, but in a playful, fond way | You are lost and need help | She is very angry and wants you to leave the room
